## Communications
## Nanostructures
Formation of Nickel Sulfide Nanoframes from Metal–Organic Frameworks with Enhanced Pseudocapacitive and Electrocatalytic Properties
From frameworks to frames: Nickel sulfide nanoframes are synthesized through the reaction between Ni-Co Prussian blue analogue nanocubes and \(S^{2-}\) ions (see scheme). Benefitting from their structural
merits including open structure and high porosity, these NiS nanoframes exhibit enhanced electrochemical properties for both supercapacitors and hydrogen evolution reaction.
